{"notes":["CODE-SIDE VERIFIED (reviewer): B1 deferred registration implemented in eka-cli cmd/plugin_registration.go — registerPluginCommands hooked into newRootCommand (after assignCommandGroups), one cobra command per manifest-declared command under the dynamic Plugins group (GroupID mechanism, cmd/help_groups.go commandGroupsFor/hasPluginCommands; the group is added only when plugin commands exist); dispatch executes eka-\u003cname\u003e \u003cargs...\u003e [user args...] under the bounded env whitelist (PATH/HOME/EKA_PLUGIN_DIR/SystemRoot — the eka-core pluginEnv mirror, never secrets) with inherited streams and propagated exit codes (DisableFlagParsing: the plugin owns its flags); G2 anti-TOCTOU — the install/update finalize writes the binary SHA-256 sidecar (.eka-\u003cname\u003e.sha256, atomic temp+rename; remove deletes it), registration verifies the binary against the sidecar, and EVERY dispatch recomputes the hash (fresh at the point of execution; the expected checksum is memoized per process); G3 — commands register only from the plugin-dir instance, every eka-* on PATH without a registry install is visibly refused with a deterministic message, PATH copies shadowing an installed plugin warn; G4 — collisions with built-ins/help/completion/other plugins refuse deterministically (first-wins in sorted order), the manifest probe is cached per process with a TTL and invalidated on reinstall (binary identity); failure semantics — probe timeout pluginProbeTimeout=2s (\u003c=2s AC), broken/hung/unverifiable plugins are skipped with a visible deterministic stderr warning, never breaking the CLI; registration and dispatch decisions memoized per process (mutex-guarded cache). Checksum sidecar format is hex-only (the req's install timestamp is documented as not persisted — the per-process TTL cache + binary identity bound staleness). Tests: 15 new hermetic tests in cmd/plugin_registration_test.go covering registration into help + landing, dispatch (args, env whitelist